">Jb 4:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 33:5\" href=\"/Job.33.5\">33:5</a>."}], "all_cited": true, "num": "b."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "c. inf. implic., always neg., <a data-ref=\"Genesis 29:8\" href=\"/Genesis.29.8\">Gn 29:8</a> go and feed them; and they said, <em>We are not able, cannot</em> (J), <a data-ref=\"Exodus 8:14\" href=\"/Exodus.8.14\">Ex 8:14</a> (P), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 29\" href=\"/Isaiah.29\">Is 29</a>;<a data-ref=\"Isaiah 11\" href=\"/Isaiah.11\">11</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.9\">Je 20:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 21:12\" href=\"/Psalms.21.12\">ψ 21:12</a> <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:13\" href=\"/Jonah.1.13\">Jon 1:13</a>."}], "all_cited": true, "num": "c."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "c. neg. = <em>may not</em> (of moral inability): <a data-ref=\"Genesis 43:32\" href=\"/Genesis.43.32\">Gn 43:32</a> (J) the Egyptians <em>might not eat</em> bread with the Hebrews; <a data-ref=\"Judges 21:18\" href=\"/Judges.21.18\">Ju 21:18</a> <em>we may not give</em> them wives; especially D, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 7:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.7.22\">Dt 7:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.17\">12:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:24\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.24\">14:24</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 16:5\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.16.5\">16:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 17:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.17.15\">17:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 22:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.22.3\">22:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:27\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.27\">28:27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:35\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.35\">35</a>."}], "num": "d."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>be able</em>, sq. impf.: <span dir=\"rtl\">אוּלַי אוּכַל נַכֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 22:6\" href=\"/Numbers.22.6\">Nu 22:6</a> (JE) <em>perchance I am able</em> (so that) <em>we smite</em> (v. Di; read perhaps <span dir=\"rtl\">נוּכַל</span> for <span dir=\"rtl\">אוּכַל</span> Ges<sup>§ 120, 1 b</sup>); <span dir=\"rtl\">לֹא יוּכְלוּ יִג